<title>UK: Saudi lifts June Arab Medium to Europe, flat to US.</title>
<headline>Saudi lifts June Arab Medium to Europe, flat to US.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has increased the price of its Arab Medium crude oil for European term customers in June by 20 cents to Dated Brent less $3.35 a barrel, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>But the state oil giant left the grade's formula for customers in the U.S. unchanged at WTI less $4.65 a barrel, they said.</p>
<p>On Monday, traders said Saudi Aramco had increased the price of Arab Light and Berri Extra Light crudes for Europe by 20 cents and Arab Heavy by 15 cents.</p>
<p>--Mark Thompson, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
